# OSINTGraph — Core

## Product

OSINT investigation platform with relational graph analysis. Works only on legally accessible open sources or analyst-provided data.

## Stack

- UI: Streamlit (`streamlit_app.py` + `streamlit/views/`)
- Backend: FastAPI + SQLite + plugins (`backend/`)
- Entry: `AGENTS.md`, `.agent/specs/001-domain-model.md`

## Domain hierarchy

`Dossier → Carnet → Entité → Source → Observation → Evidence → Relation → Hypothesis`

Legacy `workspace_id` maps to `dossier_id` during migration. Dual-write blob + relational tables until stable.

## Code rules

- Minimal diffs; no big-bang refactors
- Reuse existing backend services (`domain_client`, plugins, transforms)
- Every OSINT datum needs provenance: source, collectedAt, collectionMethod, confidence, status
- Confidence statuses: CONFIRMED, LIKELY, POSSIBLE, UNVERIFIED, CONTRADICTED
- AI output is always a hypothesis until analyst confirms

## Do not

- Add Neo4j/Celery without explicit spec
- Bypass platform auth or scrape private data
- Present AI claims as facts
- Log PII (emails, phones, tokens) in backend logs

## Planned (not built)

Neo4j, Agent-OS orchestrator, Celery queue — document as planned only.
